# What NOT to upload when building from source with `gcloud run deploy --source`.
#
# Without this file gcloud derives one from .gitignore, which would be close but
# would also skip data/raw/ai4i2020.csv. The Dockerfile copies that file, so the
# build fails without it. Being explicit here avoids that trap.

.git
.gitignore
.venv
.pytest_cache
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
tests/
models/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
.env
Makefile
README.md
requirements-dev.txt

# data/raw/ai4i2020.csv is deliberately NOT ignored. The image trains at build
# time and needs it.

# Documentation and local working files. None of this belongs in the build, and
# the design notes, demo script and export files are local only.
DESIGN_NOTES.md
TECHNICAL_DOCUMENTATION.md
docs/
submission/
.env.example
.dockerignore
